ou which marker is eaten now, while the eaten marker's arrow tells you how the sprite must face for the next leg, so every step couples local consumption with one-step lookahead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/33/code.py:33:#    The geometry is intentionally narrow and repetitive rather than highly free-form:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8e5c0c38/37/code.py:65:    class narrow while still preventing a brittle \"exactly one shape\" shortcut.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5545f144/13/code.py:80:#      current arrow, the remaining markers, and the already-painted prefix trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/28a6681f/11/code.py:30:#    - The geometry family is intentionally narrow: one top source shelf and three shaft mouths.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/5/code.py:13:# - The generator uses narrow funnel chambers so both changes are externally visible:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:11:#      color itself forms a small arrow silhouette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:14:#    - Fusion rule used here: the arrow still has an orientation, but that orientation is not a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:16:#      the matching legend corner, the arrow tells us which of the two tangent directions to take\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:19:#    - Small trace: if a TL-corner legend contains a wall-colored arrow pointing east, then for\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:22:#      step is east, it uses the counterclockwise track. The same arrow would have meant \"slide\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:28:#    - Arrow directions still come from a small discrete family (4 cardinals via 5x5 arrows, 4\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:29:#      diagonals via 6x7 arrows), avoiding excessive freedom while keeping the visual cue obvious.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:35:#      That is invalid now because legends are two-color arrow templates. The new solver matches\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:36:#      the dominant-color silhouette against 5x5 / 6x7 arrow masks.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:42:#    - Fusion-specific new assumption: the arrow direction must equal one of the two possible first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:47:#      so later-chosen 5x5 or 6x7 arrows never collide with walls.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:54:#      the legend visibly looks like an arrow rather than a dot-offset code, and the yellows stay\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:56:#    - Because the arrow matches the initial tangent at the anchor, samples make clear that the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:57:#      arrow is not a free-space motion vector: the yellows do not cut across the room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:68:#    - The chosen arrow direction equals the clockwise first step or the counterclockwise first\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:135:def _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:140:def _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr: int, dc: int) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:152:CARDINAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in CARDINAL_DIRS}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:153:DIAGONAL_TEMPLATE_MASKS = {(dr, dc): _diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc) for dr, dc in DIAGONAL_DIRS}\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:164:        patch[_cardinal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:167:    patch[_diagonal_arrow_mask(dr, dc)] = fill\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:207:def _match_arrow_direction(fill_mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:219:def _legend_arrow_info(g: np.ndarray, bg: int) -> dict[int, tuple[tuple[int, int], str]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:221:    Detect border legends and decode wall_color -> (arrow_direction, corner).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:224:    silhouette against arrow templates instead of comparing minority-color centroids.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:243:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(patch == fill)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:360:def _select_track_from_arrow(profile: dict[str, object], arrow_dir: tuple[int, int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:363:    if arrow_dir == cw_dir and arrow_dir != ccw_dir:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:365:    if arrow_dir == ccw_dir and arrow_dir != cw_dir:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:368:    cw_score = _dir_score(cw_dir, arrow_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:369:    ccw_score = _dir_score(ccw_dir, arrow_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:394:    Slide yellow pixels inside walled regions along the inner wall, using arrow legends as entry tangents.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:400:      region wall color, and that dominant color is arranged as a visible arrow silhouette.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:405:    - The legend arrow does not mean \"move straight through the room\". Instead it selects which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/88e364bc/41/code.py:410:    Key insight: The legend color still links the correct 