e same color;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:44:       3. the arrow lies exactly one blank cell beyond one frame side and overlaps that side's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:50:   - Generator builds the output state first: cup frame + detached arrow + ejected line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:51:   - Combined occupied cells of cup and arrow keep an 8-neighborhood gap from other cups/arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:54:   - The arrow is offset away from the ray, so the output line never overwrites the marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:58:   - The detached arrow is plainly visible on one closed side, so humans can see that ejection is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:65:   - Cups, arrows, and rays are kept disjoint across objects.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:69:   - No new color mapping is introduced. The arrow reuses the frame color, so the association is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:76:   - Assumption: exactly one nearby L-arrow of the same color lies one cell beyond a closed side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:77:     Guaranteed by fixed arrow templates and unique border colors per cup.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:211:def _is_l_arrow_component(cells: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:212:    \"\"\"3-cell detached arrow sprite: an L triomino inside a 2x2 bbox.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:232:def _arrow_side(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:233:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:236:    \"\"\"Infer which cup side the detached arrow marks.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:237:    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = (int(v) for v in bbox_coords(np.array(sorted(arrow_cells), dtype=int)))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:255:    - A detached same-color 3-pixel L arrow picks one closed side as the tail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:273:        arrow_candidates: list[set[tuple[int, int]]] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:276:            if _is_l_arrow_component(comp_set):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:277:                arrow_candidates.append(comp_set)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:315:            for arrow_cells in arrow_candidates:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:316:                tail_dir = _arrow_side(arrow_cells, bbox)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:363:def _attach_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:370:    \"\"\"Return a combined patch containing the frame and a detached arrow.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:378:    arrow_template = ARROW_OFFSETS[tail_dir][int(rng.integers(0, 2))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:379:    arrow_coords = [(spike[0] + dr, spike[1] + dc) for dr, dc in arrow_template]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:380:    all_coords = body_coords + arrow_coords\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:390:    for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:430:    \"\"\"Place one cup+arrow combo while preserving spacing and a clear ray to the edge.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/3dc255db/7/code.py:538:    combo_patch, spike, mouth, body_bbox_local = _attach_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/13/code.py:204:    - One full-height grey (5) separator column splits the grid into a left sprite field and a narrow right chamber.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/23/code.py:33:# - The right pane is narrowed only slightly less than the seed task: width is kept in 3..4.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/22/code.py:201:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column splits a narrow left ray pane from a wider right sprite pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/6e453dd6/6/code.py:146:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column divides the grid into a wide left sprite pane and a narrow right ray pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/7/code.py:159:    - A narrow legend strip occupies the left edge. Each 3x3 legend glyph has one trigger color at its center plus a gray shape that specifies that color's ray behavior.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/19/code.py:26:#    - `main()` launch-row detection assumed many bar colors might exist, but its real requirement is narrower:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:23:#   Walls isolate one narrow chamber, so a human can see the front maroon disappear first,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/18/code.py:293:    - Magenta walls form narrow corridors near the destination.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8f3a5a89/D1/2/code.py:54:#      examples and infer that some slits are too narrow to count as passable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:20:      - 左边起点表现为 `(row,0)=particle, (row,1)=arrow`; 右边是 `(row,W-1)=particle, (row,W-2)=arrow`;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:118:    \"\"\"Return border particles whose unique adjacent arrow pixel defines the start direction.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:183:    \"\"\"Move arrow-marked edge particles through same-color corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:186:    - bg=7, particle=6, arrow marker=2.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:188:    - Particles may appear on any of the four grid edges, each with exactly one adjacent arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:191:    - The arrow offset relative to a border particle gives its initial direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:192:    - The particle moves straight through passable cells (bg, particle, arrow).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:199:      You must first read each edge particle's adjacent arrow to recover the initial\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:630:def _place_particles_and_arrows(g: np.ndarray, starts: list[tuple[int, int, str]]) -> bool:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:631:    \"\"\"Place particles on the border and their unique adjacent arrow markers.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:633:    arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]] = set()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:641:        if (ar, ac) in arrow_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:645:        arrow_cells.add((ar, ac))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9bbf930d/4/code.py:709:    if not _place_particles_and_arrows(g, starts):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/2d0172a1/D10/1/code.py:38:#     the variant is intentionally narrow: only output shape changes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:17:#    - Combo task: each endpoint is replaced by a 3-cell blue L-arrow. The degree-2 corner is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:18:#      the tip, and the missing diagonal quadrant is the arrow's forward direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:19:#    - Each arrow tip has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker pixel in a non-blue,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:20:#      non-magenta color. Two arrows with the same marker color are one pair.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:21:#    - For one pair, the two tips lie on a common 45-degree diagonal and the arrows face each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:28:#      combo logic: blue arrows with tips at (2,2),(6,6), same red marker color, facing toward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:40:#    - Original blue-pixel grouping by diagonal is invalid: each arrow contains an incidental\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:43:#      colors attached to arrow tips.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:50:#      2. every arrow tip has exactly one adjacent non-bg, non-blue, non-magenta marker;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:51:#      3. every marker color labels exactly two arrows;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:52:#      4. paired arrows lie on one diagonal and face each other;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:57:#    - Both arrow bodies, both X branches, markers, triggers, and emitted rays must stay in-bounds\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:68:#      1. blue L-shapes identify arrow tips and directions;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:69:#      2. repeated marker colors identify which distant arrows pair up;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:144:def _arrow_cells(tip: tuple[int, int], direction: tuple[int, int]) -> set[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:156:def _parse_arrow_component(comp: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> tuple[tuple[int, int], tuple[int, int]] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:178:def _find_arrow_sources(grid: np.ndarray) -> list[dict]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:181:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:199:            parsed = _parse_arrow_component(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:203:            arrows.append({\"tip\": tip, \"direction\": direction, \"cells\": comp})\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:205:    arrows.sort(key=lambda item: item[\"tip\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:206:    return arrows\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:231:    assert dr != 0 and abs(dr) == abs(dc), \"paired arrow tips must share a diagonal\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:238:    raise AssertionError(\"paired arrows must face each other along their tip diagonal\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:265:    arrows = _find_arrow_sources(grid)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:267:    for arrow in arrows:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:268:        tip = arrow[\"tip\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:277:        marker_groups.setdefault(markers[0], []).append(arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:376:    Read marked blue arrow pairs, expand each pair into an X, and emit magenta rays from triggers touched by either branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:379:    - The background is the most common color. Active blue objects are 3-cell L-shaped arrows; the degree-2 corner is the tip and the missing diagonal quadrant gives the arrow's facing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:380:    - Each arrow tip has exactly one orthogonally adjacent marker pixel in a non-blue, non-magenta color. Two arrows with the same marker color belong together.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/db695cfb/15/code.py:384:    - For every marker-matched arrow pair, use the two tips as the endpoints of a direct diagonal and verify that the arrows