810/27/code.py:53:#    The generator is output-first. It places arrows with one-cell guard bands,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:55:#    any previous non-background payload. This guarantees that each arrow has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:56:#    exactly one adjacent non-arrow component and label-based extraction stays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:61:#    shows all three cues: the arrow points one way while the seed sits on a\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:63:#    the same geometry but cycle their colors. Other arrows reuse the same size\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:68:#    other, and each grid uses only 2-4 arrows. This prevents component merges\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:79:#    - every sample uses at least two arrow orientations,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:85:#    - All arrows share one of the known templates, up to rotation.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:87:#    - Exactly one adjacent marker component per arrow is present.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:196:def _oriented_arrow_spec(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:206:def _match_arrow_component(mask: np.ndarray) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:210:            rotated, launch_local, attach_normal = _oriented_arrow_spec(spec, direction_name)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:221:def _detect_arrow_color(grid: np.ndarray, *, bg: int) -> int | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:235:            if _match_arrow_component(local) is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:399:    Extend large marker tiles from arrow anchors, cycling colors on every repeated chunk.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:403:    - One non-background color forms several rotated arrow sprites from a small fixed template family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:404:    - Each arrow has exactly one adjacent large rectangular seed marker on a side flank, and exactly one arrow in the grid keeps its full long ray as the clue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:407:    - Read each arrow's pointing direction from its silhouette rather than from the marker attachment side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:408:    - Infer the shared seed-tile size from the compact markers, reconstruct the clue arrow's first tile, and learn a global color permutation by comparing consecutive full chunks on the long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:409:    - For every arrow, repeat its seed rectangle outward in the arrow direction until the boundary, applying one more step of the learned color cycle after each whole-tile advance; arrow pixels are never overwritten.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:412:    The task now fuses three cues: arrow shape gives direction, the payload is a large textured rectangle, and the single long example ray reveals that repetition preserves geometry but rotates colors through a fixed global cycle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:419:    arrow_color = _detect_arrow_color(g, bg=int(bg))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:420:    if arrow_color is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:423:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_color), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:424:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/27/code.py:428:    arrow_records: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53