available]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e12f9a14/6/code.py:769:            size = narrow_sizes[int(rng.integers(len(narrow_sizes)))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:21:#   - Width is restricted to the small visible set {2, 3}; that is narrow enough\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:33:#     non-background population. The generator keeps the narrow band dominant over\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/17/code.py:481:    \"\"\"Stable 15x15 narrow-band layout with a readable left-edge separator.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:32:#      combo: detect arrow-shaped mover -> read its tip direction -> read border control\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:37:#    - n is restricted to 2..4. This keeps the arrow decomposition legible and avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:57:#    - Across examples, humans can see one arrowed object, one plain target square, one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:58:#      red boundary dot, and outputs that sometimes follow the arrow and sometimes defy it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:103:def _arrow_square_info(comp: dict) -> dict | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:261:        mover_info = _arrow_square_info(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:404:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:405:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:793:    arrow_step = control_step if agree else (decoy_step if control_step == main_step else main_step)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/19/code.py:795:    tip = _choose_tip_cell(grid, mover_r, mover_c, n, STEP_TO_NAME[arrow_step])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a395ee82/12/code.py:96:#       This keeps the inference space narrow enough for ARC-style reasoning.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:51:#    Yellow and teal are confined to narrow corridors outside the destination. Teal overrides yellow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/dd6b8c4b/12/code.py:218:    - The fill order is still controlled by reachability and distance, but the fused variant exposes two nested BFS products: the full reachable background region and the narrower subset of floor cells that lie on the transport routes of the collected maroons.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/24/code.py:30:#    This makes the combo visually distinct from the original narrow markers without\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:47:  - a later horizontal gate may narrow to height 2, so it still passes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:48:  - the final horizontal gate may narrow to height 1, so the 2-high token stops\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/4/code.py:53:  - horizontal and vertical narrowings test different rectangle dimensions\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/5/code.py:28:#        original task: the black square stops because the blue river narrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:33:#      combo task: one later spiral step is narrowed below width n, so the next spiral cell becomes infeasible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:46:#    - Width variation is limited to a few one-cell bulges and one optional narrowing gate. That is enough to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:62:#    - The narrowing gate only erases part of the leading row/column of the next spiral placement, preserving\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/28/code.py:67:#    - Reachable vs stuck examples differ by a visible local narrowing on a later ring or turn. The side bulge\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_c