they thread through a narrow corridor, using alternating turn priority with a backup turn.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:298:    - Because the path is a narrow corridor, the particle keeps moving straight until the corridor wall blocks its next cell; that blocked wall cell is marked with the end color if it is background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:323:    \"\"\"Reject local rooms so the path reads as a narrow 1-2 cell corridor.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:348:    \"\"\"Build a single narrow serpentine corridor that guarantees an early fallback turn.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/5/code.py:388:    # At most one gentle width-2 bulge keeps the corridor visibly narrow instead of turning it into a room.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/41/code.py:52:  - original blocker source: river narrows below width n,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:346:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/6/code.py:347:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/37/code.py:42:#    is visible in the output as wider or narrower rectangular corridors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:22:# - Replace the old single-pixel sources with 3-cell arrowheads in the first cycle\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:23:#   color. The arrow tip is the launch cell.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:27:# - Fusion choice for the D4/D11 tension: every arrowhead must point in the same\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:30:#   `v` arrowheads, motion starts downward; if the turn bars read [L,R,R], later\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:36:# - The added symbols all use low-cardinality, human-visible geometry: arrow shape,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:46:#   replaced by 8-connected size-3 arrowhead decoding.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:48:#   new symbolic cues, so the solver now decodes the arrowheads and template glyph\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:65:#   the paint cycle, side bars are the turn sequence, and the arrow/glyph direction\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:73:#   glyph stay in the top-left template region, while arrowheads stay inside the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:81:#   has exactly one indicator, the glyph direction matches every arrow marker, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:82:#   all placed arrows are non-degenerate against legacy neighbor-priority launch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:106:def _arrow_cells(tip_r: int, tip_c: int, direction: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:113:def _decode_arrow_component(coords: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int, str] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:120:            if set(_arrow_cells(int(tip_r), int(tip_c), direction)) == comp:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:157:        f\"arrow direction {marker_dir} must agree with template glyph {global_dir}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:162:def _find_arrow_markers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:170:        decoded = _decode_arrow_component(coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:189:def _assert_arrow_markers_valid(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:196:    assert 1 <= len(markers) <= 2, f\"expected 1-2 arrow markers, got {len(markers)}\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:202:        assert tuple(sorted(_arrow_cells(tip_r, tip_c, direction))) == cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:310:    markers = _find_arrow_markers(g, int(pattern[0]), int(path_color))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:311:    _assert_arrow_markers_valid(g, markers, int(path_color), str(global_dir))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:441:    Simulate recoloring particles on a path using arrow-shaped sources plus template direction symbols.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:446:    - Start markers are 3-cell arrowheads in the first cycle color, embedded inside the path band, and a separate 2x2 block provides the terminal collision color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:450:    - Decode each arrow marker and require its pointing direction to agree with the template glyph; each particle starts from the arrow tip in that shared direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:455:    - The template now carries two independent symbolic programs at once: block colors specify the repaint cycle, and instruction marks specify both the shared launch heading and the collision-turn schedule, while the arrowheads localize the actual start tips and confirm the heading geometrically.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:592:def _collect_arrow_candidates(mask: np.ndarray, target_row: int) -> list[dict[str, object]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:605:                    cells = _arrow_cells(int(r), int(c), direction)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:638:def _place_arrow_markers(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:641:    cand_lists = [_collect_arrow_candidates(mask, int(row)) for row in target_rows]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/195c6913/22/code.py:782:    placed = _place_arrow_markers(g, mask, target_rows, int(cycle_colors[0]))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:32:     real chokepoint narrower than n and the mover always halts upstream.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:75:  human to infer \"the river gets erased behind the sliding block until the first too-narrow gate.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:383:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/30/code.py:384:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:400:    use_narrow_hint = (n == 1 and random.random() < 0.75) or (n >= 2 and not reached)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:489:    if use_narrow_hint:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:523:        if use_narrow_hint and not geo_ok:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/14/code.py:525:        if not use_narrow_hint and geo_ok != dest_ok:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:37:#      usually horizontal only: blank outer columns disappear, producing a narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/b5ca7ac4/31/code.py:50:#    - To keep the change legible, generator columns come from two narrow but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:12:#   or at the farthest reachable interior placement before a narrow gate.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:51:#   examples, it stops inside just before a narrow section. No overlapping markers or\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:296:    narrow_w = random.randint(1, n - 1)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/332f06d7/12/code.py:297:    remove = n - narrow_w\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/da515329/17/code.py:31:#   and the cropped fill stays in a narrow range, making the edge-stop + tight\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/18/code.py:349:    - Each activated blob launches a ray from its uniquely narrowest extreme side, with width 1 or 2 from that side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:15:# - This combo replaces the source object with arrow-shaped anchors and simultaneously changes the direction cue:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:16:#   the ray must follow the arrow's protruding head, not the side where the seed happens to touch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:18:#   Example: a right-facing arrow may have its seed above or below it, but the output still repeats that seed to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:24:# - Each grid uses at least two arrow orientations, so the shape cue is actually demonstrated inside one sample.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:26:# - `detect_dominant_big_component_color()` still works because arrows remain the only components with bbox >= 3x3.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:31:# - The generator is output-first: place full arrows and full rays first, then erase all but one long clue ray.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:32:# - Arrows, rays, and their 4-neighborhood guards are kept separate so two non-arrow components never merge under\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:33:#   `label_mask((grid != bg) & (grid != arrow_color))`.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:34:# - Candidate seeds are rejected if they go out of bounds, overlap, or even touch previously committed rays / arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:36:# - The crucial cue is human-visible geometry: each arrow has one protruding tip and that tip points the repetition.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:38:# - The kept pre-extended clue ray shows that the repeated payload follows the arrow orientation rather than contact.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:41:# - No ray is allowed to touch a foreign arrow or another ray, so each object stays visually isolated.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:44:# - No ordering on color ids is used. Colors only separate background / arrow anchors / payload tiles.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:47:# - For every generated arrow, the attachment side should be orthogonal to the true ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:50:# - Solver assumes each big anchor component exactly matches one rotated arrow template below.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:51:# - Solver assumes each arrow has exactly one adjacent non-arrow component (seed or pre-extended ray component).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:215:def _build_arrow_lookup() -> dict[tuple[tuple[int, ...], ...], tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:224:_ARROW_LOOKUP = _build_arrow_lookup()\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:227:def _match_arrow_direction(mask: np.ndarray) -> tuple[int, int] | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:254:def detect_arrow_component_color(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:260:    \"\"\"Choose the color whose big components best match the arrow template family.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:283:            if _match_arrow_direction(local) is not None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:295:# Extend marker rays from arrow-shaped anchors using the arrow head as the only direction cue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:298:# - One dominant non-background color forms several arrow sprites, all drawn from the same small template family.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:299:# - Each arrow touches exactly one colored marker component, and exactly one of those components may already be a long\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:302:# - Recognize the arrow's facing direction from its protruding tip, not from the marker's contact side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:304:# - Repeat that tile from its current seed position all the way to the boundary in the arrow-indicated direction,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:305:#   while preserving arrow-colored cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:308:#   fails. Only the arrow silhouette's asymmetric protrusion consistently identifies the ray direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:315:    arrow_col = detect_arrow_component_color(g, bg=bg, connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:316:    if arrow_col is None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:319:    arrow_lab, an = label_mask(g == int(arrow_col), connectivity=4)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:320:    non_mask = (g != int(bg)) & (g != int(arrow_col))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:324:        arrow_mask = arrow_lab == int(ak)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:325:        arrow_coords = np.argwhere(arrow_mask)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:326:        if arrow_coords.size == 0:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:329:        ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(arrow_coords)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:330:        local_arrow = arrow_mask[int(ar0):int(ar1) + 1, int(ac0):int(ac1) + 1]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:331:        direction = _match_arrow_direction(local_arrow)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:336:        for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:362:            protect={int(arrow_col)},\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:543:def _cells_clear_for_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:546:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:550:        if int(occ[r, c]) != 0 or bool(arrow_guard[r, c]) or bool(ray_guard[r, c]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:558:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:560:    own_arrow: set[tuple[int, int]],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:563:        if (int(r), int(c)) in own_arrow:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:567:        if bool(arrow_guard[r, c]) or bool(ray_guard[r, c]):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:572:def _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:580:    arrow_guard: np.ndarray,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:583:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:593:        arrow_cells = _component_cells(patch, (r0, c0))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:594:        if not _cells_clear_for_arrow(arrow_cells, occ, arrow_guard, ray_guard):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:612:            own_arrow = set((int(r), int(c)) for r, c in arrow_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:613:            if not _cells_clear_for_ray(ray_cells, occ, arrow_guard, ray_guard, own_arrow):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:616:            for rr, cc in arrow_cells:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:618:                out[rr, cc] = int(arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:619:            _mark_guard(arrow_guard, arrow_cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:641:    arrows: list[dict],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:645:    pre_idx = max(range(len(arrows)), key=lambda i: arrows[i][\"tiles\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:646:    if arrows[pre_idx][\"tiles\"] < _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:647:        candidates = [i for i, meta in enumerate(arrows) if meta[\"tiles\"] >= _PRE_EXT_IDEAL_TILES]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:652:    for i, meta in enumerate(arrows):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:666:        raise ValueError(f\"unsupported arrow count: {n}\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:691:    arrow_color = int(rng.choice(others))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:692:    palette = [c for c in others if c != arrow_color]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:700:    arrow_guard = np.zeros((H, W), dtype=bool)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:703:    arrows: list[dict] = []\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:705:        meta = _place_arrow_and_ray(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:713:            arrow_guard,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:716:            arrow_color,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:720:        arrows.append(meta)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/4/code.py:722:    inp = _build_input_from_output(out, arrows, bg, rng)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:164:        raise AssertionError(\"vertical cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:183:    raise AssertionError(\"horizontal cross must have one uniquely narrow end arm\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:188:    Build a red ray network by activating single-axis cross blobs whose narrowest arm is a hidden port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:196:    - The activated cross then emits a ray from the uniquely narrowest arm tip, with width 1 or 2 depending on that arm.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:199:    Key insight: Direction is encoded geometrically, not by color. The only arm end that is strictly narrower than the other three extremes is the implicit launch port.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/31/code.py:334:# - a constant narrow top arm (width 1 or 2),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/21/code.py:82:#    - Colors remain monochrome per source column and occupy only narrow cavity\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/15/code.py:57:#      least two rectangles in both the narrow-band and wide-band groups.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/53fb4810/14/code.py:51:#    therefore visually reserved for anchors, while marker/ray material stays narrow and readable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/13e47133/19/code.py:25:#   exercising the sequential-consumption rule beyond one narrow branch.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/6/code.py:50:#       or 3 source bars, and 1-tooth bars can even be narrower than before.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/6/code.py:73:#         count narrows candidates to \"1-tooth vs 2-tooth\";\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c3d4a41/14/code.py:165:        raise ValueError(\"bar base is too narrow\")\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:20:#    - New start object: a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite. Four red body pixels make the shaft/wedge and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:21:#      one yellow pixel protrudes on the firing side. The arrow tail is anchored on the boundary\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:29:#    - Example sketch: if a right-pointing arrow starts near the left edge, the first leg goes\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:35:#    - Direction freedom is limited to the four cardinals and one arrow family, so the start cue is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:44:#      above it. That is false now, so start detection must match the arrow geometry instead.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:51:#    - New solver assumption: exactly one arrow exists; its red body has area 4; it has exactly one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:55:#    - Objects are still placed output-first. The generator paints the arrow, then for each active\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:62:#    - The arrow makes the initial direction visible without reading color ids. Horizontal starts\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:76:#      \"read direction from the arrow, then follow repeated clockwise turns.\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:95:# --- Start arrow ---\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:579:    Build a red activation network whose first launch comes from a small arrow and whose rays curl clockwise into spirals.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:584:    - The start marker is no longer a bottom stem; it is a boundary-anchored red arrow sprite with one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:588:    - Recolor the whole start arrow red, then launch a ray from the yellow tip in the direction implied\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:589:      by the arrow shape.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:597:    - Two cues must be read together: the arrow geometry gives the initial direction, and the repeated\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/5961cc34/9/code.py:604:    # --- STEP 1) Detect the start arrow sprite and infer the initial direction ---\n/home/lixinyu/s