er_arrow.append(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:218:                \"color\": int(arrow[\"color\"]),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:219:                \"start\": arrow[\"start\"],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:220:                \"order_key\": arrow[\"order_key\"],\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:226:        \"per_arrow\": per_arrow,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:227:        \"erased_total\": int(sum(len(a[\"erased_cells\"]) for a in per_arrow)),\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:235:    Fire arrows in increasing distance-to-center order.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:237:    Reflection geometry matches the original task, but all arrows share one mutable wall set:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:238:    when a wall pixel is touched, that pixel is erased and later arrows no longer see it.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:283:        pts = _arrow_points_from_start(int(start[0]), int(start[1]), int(dr), int(dc))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:311:    per_arrow = ordered_meta[\"per_arrow\"]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:312:    first_erased = len(per_arrow[0][\"erased_cells\"]) if per_arrow else 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:313:    second_erased = len(per_arrow[1][\"erased_cells\"]) if len(per_arrow) > 1 else 0\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:345:    arrows, _arrow_cells = _detect_arrows(grid, bg=0)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:346:    if len(arrows) != 2:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:348:    arrows_sorted = sorted(arrows, key=lambda a: a[\"order_key\"])\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/7/code.py:349:    if arrows_sorted[0][\"start\"] == arrows_sorted[1][\"start\"]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:10:# - The shared anchor color now forms several small arrow blobs instead of plus-like symmetric blobs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:11:# - Each arrow is one of a few fixed templates, rotated to point U/D/L/R.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:12:# - Each arrow still owns exactly one colored seed tile and one grid keeps one ray pre-extended.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:14:#   (clockwise from the pointing direction), while the arrow's own facing direction tells us where the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:15:#   ray should go. Example: a right-pointing arrow has its seed directly below it, but the seed repeats\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:17:#   we must read the arrow shape and project \"right\".\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:24:# - Each generated grid uses at least two arrow orientations so the orientation cue is actually visible.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:26:# - detect_dominant_big_component_color still works because arrows remain the only components with both\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:35:#   wrong arrow and the solver sees exactly one adjacent non-arrow component per arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:37:#   existing arrow-neighborhood guard cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:39:# - Human-solvable cue: arrows visibly point one way while their seed sits on a different side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:40:# - The kept pre-extended ray demonstrates that the repeated pattern follows the arrow orientation, not\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/53fb4810/D4/1/code.py:44:# - Rays do not overlap arrows and do not touch foreign arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/