w(H, W, arrow_a, wall_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/19/code.py:541:    secondary = _plan_collision_arrow(H, W, arrow_b, primary)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/4/code.py:37:#    - 原 `is_arrow_pts` / `arrow_dir_and_start` 假设源面积为 3 且 bbox 为 2x2；融合后完全失效，删除。\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/142ca369/4/code.py:38:#    - 原 `arrow_cells` 扣除源对象、其余非背景当墙 的分类思想仍可保留，但前提变为：\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/16b78196/12/code.py:58:    - each continuation uses a strip that is 1 cell narrower than the previous piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/4c7dc4dd/13/code.py:40:#    The rule family is narrowed to symmetry transforms because that is the most\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/25/code.py:29:#    one-cell teeth, concave bites, narrow bridges, and visible staircase seams. The output still\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/f560132c/25/code.py:361:    - The piece silhouettes are highly irregular: tabs, bites, narrow bridges, and staircase-like borders are expected.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/7ed72f31/16/code.py:67:#     - Payload cells lie on a narrow ring around the cross, so the local geometry\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/43/code.py:36:#      - fixed narrow width 5 and heights 5..8,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/26/code.py:34:#      single-pixel fillers, while avoiding overfitting to a narrower orientation test than the combo\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/47/code.py:35:#     - The family is intentionally narrowed to one clear layout instead of the full\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/30/code.py:30:#     - The rectangle stays narrow and portrait like the source task, so the family still looks like\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:20:# - The moving marker is no longer a 1-cell-thick line. It is a fixed 3x3 arrow sprite:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:25:# - The destination marker is an identical arrow sprite of the same color, translated further\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:26:#   along the arrow's pointing direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:27:# - To make \"direction from shape\" necessary, the arrow is attached only to a side orthogonal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:32:#   Variant logic: an arrow attached above may still point right, so the container moves right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:33:#   The solver must read the arrow shape, then find the matching arrow destination along that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:37:# - The arrow has only four orientations and one fixed size, so the new degree of freedom is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:47:#   the subset of pixels closest to the border. With an arrow sprite, that \"closest layer only\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:48:#   extraction would lose most of the arrow and break matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:50:#   shape, matches it against four fixed arrow templates, and derives direction from that match.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:53:# - Each generated object reserves a rectangle covering: input container, input arrow, destination\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:54:#   arrow, moved container, and moved arrow. Reserved rectangles are packed with a 1-cell margin,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:56:# - The destination arrow is always at least one background cell away from the head arrow, which\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:60:# - Because the arrow is orthogonally attached, the changed mechanism is visible in every mover:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:65:# - Only three object types remain on the board: container, source arrow, destination arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:66:#   The arrow is compact (3x3), monochrome, and separated from other assemblies by background.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:70:#   cue that the viewer has to infer is the arrow orientation itself.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:114:def _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h: int, outer_w: int, attach_side: str, anchor: int) -> tuple[int, int]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:124:def _stamp_arrow(grid: np.ndarray, tl: tuple[int, int], direction: str, color: int) -> None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:141:    Move bordered containers toward same-colored arrow destinations, charging grey cells to orange.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:144:    - The source marker is a 3x3 arrow sprite, not a line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:145:    - Direction is derived from the arrow's normalized shape, not from which side of the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:146:      container the arrow touches.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:147:    - The container and arrow translate toward the nearest matching arrow destination along\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:148:      the arrow direction, capped by the number of grey interior cells.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:342:        head_r, head_c = _arrow_tl_relative(outer_h, outer_w, attach_side, anchor)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:442:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (hr, hc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:443:        _stamp_arrow(grid, (dr, dc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/271d71e2/D4/2/code.py:474:        _stamp_arrow(expected, (nhr, nhc), s[\"direction\"], HEAD_COLOR)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/14/code.py:37:# - The rectangle stays portrait and narrow (6x5), close to the original task's dense\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/1/code.py:46:#   sprite of the wrong contact-length class. Position alone only narrows the search;\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/36/code.py:300:    - The puzzle is no longer solved in one placement pass: color first tells which scraps belong together, then color semantics narrow the vertical band, and finally the ordered row layout resolves which same-band chamber each assembled subcomponent occupies.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/11/code.py:17:#    To keep the rule visible but not underconstrained, the output family is narrowed to two small\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/e8686506/35/code.py:72:#       overlap, and the narrow five-column layout keeps the assembled pattern easy to parse.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/12/code.py:259:    - The informative object is an extreme-aspect-ratio band, either narrow-horizontal or narrow-vertical; the third color is padding only.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/269e22fb/30/code.py:207:    - The grid itself is a long narrow window: either 5x15..18 or 15..18x5.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/11/code.py:270:    Draw red outer outlines, but count both true holes and deep narrow indentations when choosing the recolor tier.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/37/code.py:29:#      skipped (<= 10), narrow-halo (11-15), and wide-halo (>= 16).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/2c181942/13/code.py:98:#      detached components. This gives the learner repeated evidence that color narrows the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/16b78196/D8/1/code.py:51:    - that cavity spans a strip exactly 1 cell narrower than the previous piece.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/35ab12c3/D10/1/code.py:19:#   The change is narrow: distractors, colors, shadow mechanics, and spacing remain the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/34/code.py:21:#      3) a deep narrow indentation that opens to the shell bbox edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/34/code.py:279:      by a green nested object, and some shells instead expose a deep narrow notch from one bbox edge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/34/code.py:289:      cavity: an empty enclosed hole, a green nested core, and a deep narrow indentation are all\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:56:#   - Every generated grid contains at least one narrow frame and at least one wide\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:82:#   - The generator rejects layouts that cannot fit both narrow and wide frames under\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:95:#   - Only four colors appear in outputs: yellow background, blue narrow frames, teal\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:286:        \"narrow_count\": 0,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:303:            metrics[\"narrow_count\"] += 1\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:320:    num_narrow = random.randint(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[0], min(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[1], num_components - 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:330:    thicknesses = [NARROW_THICKNESS] * num_narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:331:    thicknesses.extend(random.choice(wide_choices) for _ in range(num_components - num_narrow))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/14/code.py:394:        if metrics[\"narrow_count\"] < 1 or metrics[\"wide_count\"] < 1:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/aa4ec2a5/12/code.py:55:#    one-pixel 8-neighborhood outlines remain disjoint. Each group is anchored in a narrow column\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:704:def _place_docked_trains(base, bg, regions, arrow_color):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:725:            output[r0 + ir, c0 + ic] = arrow_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:740:def _scatter_trains(base, bg, regions, trains, arrow_color):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:750:        input_grid[ir, ic] = arrow_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:793:    arrow_candidates = [c for c in range(8) if c != bg and c not in stripe_colors]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:794:    if not arrow_candidates:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:796:    arrow_color = random.choice(arrow_candidates)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:798:    placed = _place_docked_trains(base, bg, regions, arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/1/code.py:803:    input_grid = _scatter_trains(base, bg, regions, trains, arrow_color)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:10:#    with two couplers could only map to one size-2 station. Here the same train first narrows to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e4f6532/D4/3/code.py:78:    Key insight: coupler count is no longer sufficient by itself; it only narrows the search, and the region-stripe palette carried on the train resolves which equal-sized station is the true dock.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/33/code.py:54:#    narrow connectors, so the output reads as one coherent serpentine region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/28/code.py:390:      generated tasks connector color already narrows the candidate set, and the final validation\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/16/code.py:41:#   - Original assumption: frame sizes live in a narrow band. Broken here because large-vs-small frame\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/a25697e4/9/code.py:20:#   The family is intentionally narrow: one frame, 2 or 3 tools, strictly decreasing\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:13:     an explicit 3-pixel arrow inside each source sprite.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:15:     Sources replace the single interior pixel with a 3-pixel arrowhead made from the transfer color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:18:       new: source.arrow points right, exactly one destination lies to the right of that source ->\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:19:            copy source.arrow color into that destination center\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:20:     The path still tells us which two sprites are destinations; the arrow only decides source->target.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:23:   - The arrow alphabet is limited to four global directions: up/down/left/right.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:24:   - Each sample contains exactly two arrow-bearing sources so the symbol is repeated and decodable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:33:     The arrow therefore uses only the center and corners, leaving cardinal border cells untouched.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:43:     by the grey path, while the deleted source sprites visibly contain arrowheads that point toward\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:46:     solver to use the arrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:49:   - Only box sprites are used in this variant. That keeps the arrow symbols readable and avoids\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:55:   - The color transferred to a destination is simply the arrow color shown inside the matching source.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:59:   - Assumption: every arrow source is a full 3x3 box with one of four known 3-pixel patterns.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:136:    Source sprites have a 3-pixel inner arrow pattern.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:192:def _decode_arrow(sprite: dict) -> str | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:193:    \"\"\"Return the arrow direction for a full 3x3 source sprite, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:220:    Transfer source arrow colors into the two path-connected bordered sprites, keeping only those destinations.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:225:    - Non-destination boxes are either plain distractors or full 3x3 source boxes whose interior 3-pixel arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:230:    - For every arrow-bearing source sprite, decode its pointing direction and identify which destination lies in\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:231:      that direction from the source. Copy the source arrow color into that destination center pixel.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:297:        direction = _decode_arrow(sp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:301:        assert len(cands) == 1, \"each source arrow should identify exactly one destination\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:336:def _make_arrow_patch(border_color: int, arrow_color: int, direction: str) -> np.ndarray:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:339:        p[1 + dr, 1 + dc] = arrow_color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:571:def _place_arrow_source(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:574:    arrow_color: int,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:585:        patch = _make_arrow_patch(border_color, arrow_color, target_dir)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:664:    if not _place_arrow_source(input_grid, border_colors[2], source_colors[0], 0, dest_centers):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/d35bdbdc/D15/2/code.py:666:    if not _place_arrow_source(input_grid, border_colors[3], source_colors[1], 1, dest_centers):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/28/code.py:76:#   center alignment is not explainable by simply following the legend arrow. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D5/3/code.py:39:# - The variant is intentionally narrow: corridor geometry, turn shapes, and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/abc82100/39/code.py:78:   - Restricting the generator to a narrow family of odd hollow frames makes the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/20/code.py:367:    - Each structure is a rotated nested comb: a tall outer cavity contains a narrower inner cavity, and the true teeth are spaced apart (`101` or `10101`).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D2/1/code.py:68:#    notice those narrow edge pixels. We also force at least one two-tone\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/8b9c3697/9/code.py:299:    - Rank those candidate red plugs from smaller area to larger area, rank sockets from narrower span to wider span, then dock them in that order; all traversed cells become black and every other red vanishes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D2/0/code.py:22:#       into the narrow side column. In this variant, adjacent corner-style exits are dead:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D2/0/code.py:49:#     - Therefore the variant redefines horizontal reachability narrowly: the drop column must\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D2/0/code.py:95:    shafts plus longer flat shelves, so narrow step chutes no longer connect basins.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:207:    Move a compact water plug through a wall-bounded corridor until the corridor ends or narrows.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:212:    - The source plug starts at one endpoint of the reachable corridor. Downstream sections may bend and may later narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/1/code.py:218:    - Relocate the plug to the last reachable placement before the corridor terminates or becomes too narrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/12/code.py:22:#      rows below the left bar, their thick diagonal halos overlap in the center and leave a narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/cb2d8a2c/12/code.py:39:#      D10/0 requires overlapping halos and narrow channels, so the generator now chooses very\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D1/2/code.py:16:#    \"air\" is no longer the transport medium. Instead, color 8 marks a narrow pipe network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D10/2/code.py:143:    \"\"\"Move each magenta particle along aligned narrow corridors.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/27/code.py:19:#    - D17/0 is narrowed by the fusion description: only the unmarked spectator lanes turn grey, rather than\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D17/0/code.py:64:#   subcomponents reserve their own narrower interval in their matched bar.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/38007db0/D5/2/code.py:90:#     much shorter/narrower than the original single-column lattice\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D3/1/code.py:240:    - The remaining colors form fixed shelves, walls, and narrow reservoirs anchored to the lower half.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/0/code.py:28:#    - The change is intentionally narrow: only D20 changes. Water motion,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D13/0/code.py:34:#   - The geometry is kept to one family of adjacent basins with a narrow transfer\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:28:#    particle still sits on the border, but it now has one dedicated adjacent arrow-marker\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:45:#    is rotated by 0/90/180/270 degrees and every start gets an explicit arrow marker. This\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:52:#    - Treating only {BG, PARTICLE} as passable would make the arrow marker act like a wall.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:66:#    Using one dedicated arrow color avoids overloading corridor colors. Markers only appear\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:74:#    - Each movable particle is on the border and has exactly one 4-neighbor arrow marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:75:#    - The arrow marker color appears only in these local start pairs.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:121:    \"\"\"Return border particles with a unique adjacent arrow marker.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9bbf930d/D15/2/code.py:149:    \"\"\"Move particles through same-color corridors; initial direction comes from edge arrows.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D2/0/code.py:120:    - Color only narrows the candidate pool; the real stencil is the same-colored motif shape that\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D20/1/code.py:18:#      original: water spills from the right source into the narrow central basin; the untouched left\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D4/1/code.py:231:    narrow_rows = rng.randint(0, min(2, 9 - source_top))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D4/1/code.py:236:        cols = [9] if r < source_top + narrow_rows else [8, 9]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7c66cb00/D4/1/code.py:62:  Widths stay in a narrow range and fills remain unique, preventing ambiguity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/28a6681f/D6/0/code.py:40:#    - The basin network stays small: a narrow basin beside a wider basin, separated by\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:26:#    - Only two opening sizes are used: 2 -> narrow, 3 -> wide. This is enough to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:50:#      and often mixes narrow + wide openings in the same grid for contrast.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:695:    narrow_idx: int | None = None\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:696:    narrow_candidates = [i for i, available in enumerate(available_per_block) if i != wide_idx and 2 in available]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:697:    if block_count >= 2 and narrow_candidates and rng.random() < 0.8:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:698:        narrow_idx = narrow_candidates[int(rng.integers(len(narrow_candidates)))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D5/2/code.py:704:        elif i == narrow_idx:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/67e490f4/D17/1/code.py:436:    \"\"\"Choose the narrowest 1- or 2-column layout that fits vertically.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/58f5dbd5/D16/1/code.py:63:# - The legend uses only a narrow 2-column corner strip with blank rows between pairs, so it is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/16/code.py:55:#    - The crop is equally visible because outputs are narrower and shorter than the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D13/2/code.py:25:#    - The solver still supports all original collision branches. The generator narrows the placement space to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e12f9a14/D16/2/code.py:56:#        narrow slit -> dense beam\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D7/1/code.py:52:#     - For multi-cup inputs the generator constrains cup centers to a narrow shared row band\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:5:\"\"\"Variant of 3dc255db with arrow-indicated ejection direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:17:     L-shaped arrow is attached near the tail side. The arrow is 8-connected to\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:20:   - The arrow is placed so the old bbox-based spike heuristic is no longer safe:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:21:     the merged border component's outer bbox includes the arrow, so the cup body\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:22:     must be recovered by identifying and removing that arrow candidate first.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:25:     cup has a small same-color arrow above it. The merged component's top edge is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:26:     now widened by the arrow, so \"unique top-edge spike\" is no longer reliable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:27:     The new solver removes the 3-cell arrow candidate, observes the arrow lies\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:34:   - Each cup always has exactly one arrow, and the arrow always uses the cup's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:36:   - The arrow may lean to either perpendicular side of the ray, so the samples do\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:41:     This is false now because the arrow is merged into the same 8-connected\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:44:   - Original mouth flood is still valid, but only after stripping the arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:49:       4. derive direction from which side the arrow lies on relative to that cup.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:51:     such valid arrow candidate. The generator enforces that.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:55:     same-color arrow offset near the tail side.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:56:   - The arrow is kept off the direct ejection path, so the output line never\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:57:     overwrites the arrow.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:58:   - Placement checks use the combined cup+arrow patch, so arrows do not overlap\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:62:   - Humans can see a cup plus a small same-color arrow near one side. The output\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:65:   - This does not degenerate to the original rule because the arrow is merged\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:70:   - The arrow stays adjacent to its own cup and uses the same border color, so it\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:76:   - No new color mapping is introduced. The arrow reuses the cup border color.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:81:   - Assumption: each processed border component has one removable 3-cell L arrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:83:   - Assumption: the arrow lies completely beyond exactly one side of the cup\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:84:     body's bbox. Guaranteed by generator's fixed arrow templates.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:85:   - Assumption: after removing the arrow, the cup body still has one spike on the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:86:     arrow-indicated side. Guaranteed because the underlying cup body is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:152:def _enumerate_arrow_candidates(border_set: set[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[set[tuple[int, int]]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:168:def _arrow_side(arrow_cells: set[tuple[int, int]], cup_bbox: tuple[int, int, int, int]) -> str | None:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:169:    ar0, ac0, ar1, ac1 = bbox_coords(np.array(sorted(arrow_cells), dtype=int))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:201:    - Each cup border component includes a same-color 3-pixel arrow marker.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:203:    - The side on which the arrow sits determines the ejection direction.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:222:            for arrow_cells in _enumerate_arrow_candidates(border_set):\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:223:                cup_set = border_set - arrow_cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:228:                tail_dir = _arrow_side(arrow_cells, cup_bbox)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:403:def _attach_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:411:    \"\"\"Expand the original cup patch with a same-color 3-cell arrow.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:413:    arrow_template = ARROW_OFFSETS[direction][int(rng.integers(0, 2))]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:414:    arrow_coords = [(spike[0] + dr, spike[1] + dc) for dr, dc in arrow_template]\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:416:    all_coords = border_coords + arrow_coords\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:425:    for r, c in arrow_coords:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/3dc255db/D2/2/code.py:560:    patch, spike, mouth, cup_bbox_local = _attach_arrow(\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/80a900e0/D12/0/code.py:23:#     only checkerboard are stripped away. The returned board may be shorter or narrower.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:259:    - No red/green marker bars remain. Instead, one control-color chain occupies the bottom two rows: a tail-only start node, a pass-through arrow node in the middle, and a terminal arrow node at the end.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/9aaea919/30/code.py:262:    - The tail-only lane is the source A, the middle pass-through arrow lane is the bridge B, and the terminal arrow lane is the final target C.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D8/1/code.py:40:#    Regions are 13x8, 13x8, 13x9 in each row. The source motif is kept narrow so its\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D8/1/code.py:41:#    largest 2x scale fits inside the narrowest region. Anchor placement prefers positions\n/home/li