able in 2-3 examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:56:#     That becomes wrong here because all frames have holes but narrow ones must stay blue.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:145:    - Recolor only wide frames (thickness >= 2) to teal (8); narrow one-pixel frames stay blue (1).\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:242:    num_narrow = random.randint(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[0], min(NARROW_COUNT_RANGE[1], num_components - 1))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:248:    thicknesses = [NARROW_THICKNESS] * num_narrow\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/aa4ec2a5/D14/1/code.py:249:    thicknesses.extend(random.choice(wide_choices) for _ in range(num_components - num_narrow))\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D2/0/code.py:31:# - To keep the new path visibly distinct, the right pane cannot stay too narrow. The seed\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D2/2/code.py:153:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column divides the grid into a left sprite area and a narrow right chamber.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/e8686506/D4/1/code.py:12:#         and drawn from a narrow zigzag family, so the frame bitmap itself is symmetric across both axes.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D1/3/code.py:14:#    - The comb/bracket structures stay unchanged: a single opening side leads into a narrow cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D5/2/code.py:442:    \"\"\"Carve a narrow background fjord from the left edge without disconnecting the path.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D8/2/code.py:111:    - A single full-height grey (5) separator column splits the grid into a wide left pane and a narrow right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/0/code.py:33:#   therefore mirrored too: left becomes the narrow ray zone, right becomes the wide sprite\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/0/code.py:115:    - A full-height grey (5) separator column splits a narrow left pane from a wider right pane.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D9/3/code.py:45:#      To keep the new rule human-readable, the generator narrows the path into\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/1/code.py:30:#    - A pure row/column swap would make the grid too narrow for 2-5 side-by-side sprites if\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D1/1/code.py:53:#    - Bottom pane height is kept in 2-4 rows, mirroring the original narrow \"receiving\" side and\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:25:#     - Variant: the matched red is intentionally narrower than the socket, so the old sweep would\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8b9c3697/D4/3/code.py:54:#       identical to the old narrow trail.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D2/0/code.py:406:    \"\"\"Carve a narrow bg separator from the left edge without disconnecting path.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D6/1/code.py:68:#     narrower and contain only the framed region\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D3/0/code.py:58:#    narrow-hole emitters keep the alternating gap pattern. This keeps the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D17/2/code.py:21:#    one-column slice creates a visibly narrow bridge through the obstacle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D17/2/code.py:30:#    Only one bridge gap is added, always narrow and always near the separator's\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D17/2/code.py:269:    Simulate cycle-colored particles on a single path band whose separator may contain a narrow bridge.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:11:#     it is the corridor geometry: narrow rows, tighter overlaps, and more\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:21:#   - Width is restricted to the small visible set {2, 3}. That is narrow enough\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/195c6913/D10/0/code.py:53:#     inside an already narrow