{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/10/codegen_prompts/3.md\"","aggregated_output":"你要为一个新的 ARC-AGI 风格题目实现代码。代码文件必须包含 `main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray` 和 `generate_input() -> np.ndarray`。\n\n## 新题位置\n\n- 描述目录：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed1583749884/10`\n- 题号：`3`\n- 目标代码路径：`/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/combo_new/seed1583749884/10/3.py`\n\n## 新题描述\n\n<new_puzzle index=\"3\">\n- `description`：将网格中相邻的同色像素对连接为条带，连接方向由像素对的相对位置决定，然后在条带两端绘制箭头标记。\n\n- `Input structure`：\n  - 背景为 Black。\n  - 网格中散布着若干彩色单像素点（使用 Red、Blue、Green 等颜色），每种颜色恰好出现两个像素。\n  - 同色的两个像素在水平或垂直方向上对齐。\n\n- `Rule`：\n  - 对每对同色像素，用该颜色填充两者之间的所有背景像素，形成一条直线条带。\n  - 在条带的两端各绘制一个垂直于条带方向的一像素延伸（使用 Yellow），形成\"T\"形箭头端。\n  - 保持非配对区域的像素不变。\n\n- `Key insight`：同色像素对定义了条带的端点；条带方向自动由对齐方向决定，而箭头的朝向总是垂直于条带——两者共同构成了完整的视觉连接图案。\n</new_puzzle>\n\n## 机制相似参考题\n\n下面参考题由本地相似度流程自动选择：先用 `annotations`/docstring/代码特征抽取机制标签，再按机制相似度、文本相似度和代码特征相似度重排，并用 MMR 做去重。优先学习这些题的对象识别方式、随机生成器约束、边界条件处理，不要照搬旧题规则。\n\n已选参考：train/e048c9ed, train/465b7d93, eval/dbff022c, train/963c33f8, train/3bd292e8, train/84551f4c, eval/8f3a5a89, train/bae5c565\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"e048c9ed\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2827\nmechanism=0.3735\nlexical=0.0237\ncode_feature=0.2000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, object:line_segment, object:marker, relation:aligned, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/e048c9ed.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/e048c9ed.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nAdd a quantity-color label in the top marker column for each horizontal bar.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a black background and one non-background marker pixel in the top row.\n- Below the marker row, every non-empty source row contains one solid monochrome horizontal bar to the left of the marker column.\n- Source rows are staggered every other row.\n\nRule\n- Copy the input grid.\n- For each source bar, read its quantity as the bar length.\n- Paint the quantity color in the marker column on the same row as the bar:\n  2->1, 3->4, 4->9, 5->6.\n\nKey insight\n- The grey marker supplies the result column, while each bar supplies a small quantity with a fixed color code.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"grey top-row marker column and lower monochrome horizontal bars on black background\",\n  \"transform\": \"for each bar row, add one pixel in the marker column; its color is (n*n) mod 10 where n = min(bar length minus one, first bar row plus zero-based order among the every-other source rows)\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"465b7d93\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2572\nmechanism=0.2846\nlexical=0.0185\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:line_segment, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/465b7d93.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/465b7d93.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nMove the small colored sprite into the hollow frame by stretching its shape to the frame interior.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- There are exactly two foreground colors: one forms a complete rectangular\n  one-pixel-thick frame, and the other forms one 4-connected sprite outside it.\n- The frame interior is initially background.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the original sprite from its outside location.\n- Map the sprite bbox to the frame interior bbox, sending bbox extremes to\n  interior extremes.\n- Draw straight horizontal or vertical segments between mapped positions of\n  adjacent sprite pixels, then fill any enclosed background region inside\n  those drawn segments.\n\nKey insight:\nThe outside sprite is a miniature line/fill diagram for the frame interior,\nnot a bitmap to scale by block replication.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_to_match\",\n  \"src\": \"small colored sprite s outside the frame\",\n  \"dst\": \"hollow rectangular frame interior d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"unique s maps to unique d; s.bbox extremes align to d.bbox extremes\",\n  \"transform\": \"clear s; stretch s into d by mapping bbox extremes, drawing 4-adjacent segments, and filling enclosed regions\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"dbff022c\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2685\nmechanism=0.2840\nlexical=0.0172\ncode_feature=0.6000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, operation:flood_fill, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/dbff022c.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/dbff022c.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nFill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.\n- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.\n\nRule:\n- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.\n- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.\n- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.\n\nKey insight: The palette's edge position and orientation determine reading direction; border colors in the palette uniquely key into fill colors.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"summary\": \"Use a color palette legend on the grid edge to fill sprites' interiors based on their border color mapping.\",\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"hollow sprites with colored borders s\",\n  \"dst\": \"interior of same sprite d\",\n  \"match_cond\": \"d.fill_color == palette_lookup(s.border_color)\",\n  \"path\": \"\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"\",\n  \"transform\": \"fill d with palette[s.border_color]\",\n  \"symbol_instructions\": \"palette is 2xN or Nx2 block on grid edge; read direction based on edge position: top edge reads top-to-bottom, bottom edge reads bottom-to-top, left edge reads left-to-right; first row/column is border color, second is fill color\",\n  \"multi_step\": \"Step 1: locate 2xN or Nx2 palette legend on grid edge; Step 2: build color mapping (border -> fill) based on reading direction; Step 3: for each hollow sprite, lookup border color in palette and fill interior with corresponding fill color\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    \"color-mapping\",\n    \"lookup-table\",\n    \"flood-fill\",\n    \"border-detection\"\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"The challenge is correctly reading the palette legend based on its edge position and orientation\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"4\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"963c33f8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2503\nmechanism=0.2915\nlexical=0.0201\ncode_feature=0.4000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:connected_components, object:line_segment, object:marker, relation:between, relation:direction, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/963c33f8.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/963c33f8.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nDrop the columns of the top marker downward, stopping blue-ended columns on grey obstacles and letting maroon-ended columns pass to the bottom.\n\nInput structure\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The most numerous non-background color forms stationary grey obstacle pixels.\n- The other two colors form a single 3x3 top-edge marker whose top two rows\n  are maroon and whose bottom row contains maroon or blue control pixels.\n\nRule\n- Erase the top marker.\n- Treat each marker column as a vertical drop retaining its three colors.\n- A column whose bottom control pixel is blue stops immediately above the\n  first grey pixel below that column, or bottom-aligns if none exists.\n- Contiguous maroon-ended columns pass through obstacles and bottom-align;\n  if such a run has a clear down-right slide from a grey ledge, shift the\n  run one column right before bottom-aligning.\n- When a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear\n  the rest of the marker-width gap in that bottom bar.\n\nKey insight\n- The bottom row of the top marker is a control strip: blue cells mean\n  \"stick to the first obstacle,\" while maroon cells mean \"fall through.\"\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"move_along_path\",\n  \"src\": \"columns of the 3x3 maroon/blue marker on the top edge; the bottom cell of each column is the control pixel\",\n  \"path\": \"vertical drop in each marker column; blue-ended columns stop above the first grey obstacle below, while maroon-ended runs pass through to the bottom with a one-column right slide from a clear grey ledge\",\n  \"trajectory\": \"copy each three-pixel marker column intact; contiguous maroon-ended columns are tested as one run for the slide\",\n  \"dst\": \"settled positions on the same canvas after erasing the top marker\",\n  \"transform\": \"if a maroon-ended drop lands through a grey bar on the bottom edge, clear the rest of the marker-width gap in that bar; leave other grey obstacles fixed\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"5\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"3bd292e8\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.2301\nmechanism=0.2422\nlexical=0.0273\ncode_feature=0.5000\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:line_segment, relation:adjacent, relation:between, relation:direction\n</similarity>\n<paths>\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
